{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">Hardcoded colors plus reactive dark-mode overrides never stop growing — every new component is a new place an override can be missing.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Name colors by role (<code>--color-surface</code>, <code>--color-ink</code>), reference the token everywhere, and redefine the token set once per theme at the root — components need zero changes to support a new theme.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">A two-layer token system (primitive values aliased to semantic roles) scales further, but the real win is structural: the theming decision moves from "asked per component" to "asked once at the root."</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
